Rejected experiment:
An initial implementation intercepted every cudaMemcpy/cudaMemcpyAsync inside
runtime adapters. Doitgen then emitted 42,030 events for its repeated library
calls, perturbing the measured program. This design was removed. Its rejected
diagnostic was:
  POLYGEIST_GPU_REGION_TIMING region=12473179153129242121 compute_device_ms=1373.509409 memory_device_ms=456.611808 e2e_host_ms=1856.072000 compute_wall_ms=1196.931648 memory_wall_ms=262.548128 host_device_ms=0.079744 host_wall_ms=0.018560 alloc_device_ms=1.122848 alloc_wall_ms=1.128160 free_device_ms=0.938688 free_wall_ms=0.906304 h2d_device_ms=4.677920 h2d_wall_ms=4.583904 d2h_device_ms=9.246816 d2h_wall_ms=9.187552 d2d_device_ms=440.625536 d2d_wall_ms=246.742208 h2h_device_ms=0.000000 h2h_wall_ms=0.000000 markers=42030

Measurement boundary:
The accepted implementation classifies compiler-visible GPU memory operations
at arbitrary structured positions, including inside a compute loop. Work hidden
inside an opaque external CUDA library remains charged to the surrounding
compute region. Exact internal attribution would require a separate CUPTI
activity-tracing mode; adding per-call CUDA events is intentionally rejected.
